1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,562
Hi, Michelle.

2
00:00:03,562 --> 00:00:04,730
Hello, Harry.

3
00:00:04,730 --> 00:00:07,044
It's nice to see you again.

4
00:00:07,044 --> 00:00:07,316
Hello.

5
00:00:07,316 --> 00:00:08,736
Hi, Susan.

6
00:00:08,736 --> 00:00:12,198
We have both been excited about seeing you

7
00:00:12,198 --> 00:00:13,912
and having lunch with you today.

8
00:00:13,912 --> 00:00:18,376
Michelle picked these flowers out for you.

9
00:00:18,376 --> 00:00:18,768
Daddy, can we go soon?

10
00:00:18,768 --> 00:00:22,309
We're going to go to lunch in a few minutes, honey.

11
00:00:22,309 --> 00:00:23,824
But I'm thirsty.

12
00:00:23,824 --> 00:00:30,351
OK. You go out and get a drink of water at the fountain.

13
00:00:30,351 --> 00:00:32,280
The fountain is over there, Michelle.

14
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:39,306
Near the Exit sign.

15
00:00:39,306 --> 00:00:40,490
Thank you.

16
00:00:40,490 --> 00:00:42,692
Michelle is a little shy.

17
00:00:42,692 --> 00:00:48,199
I used to be that way when I was her age.

18
00:00:48,199 --> 00:00:50,131
Harry, if Michelle doesn't want to go,

19
00:00:50,131 --> 00:00:51,585
we don't have to.

20
00:00:51,585 --> 00:00:52,545
She'll be fine.

21
00:00:52,545 --> 00:00:52,865
Remember,

22
00:00:52,865 --> 00:00:57,272
I haven't dated any one else since her mother died.

23
00:00:57,272 --> 00:00:59,225
This is a little difficult for her.

24
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:00,269
Are you ready to go?

25
00:01:00,269 --> 00:01:02,877
Yes. But could you wait one minute?

26
00:01:02,877 --> 00:01:04,917
I have a call to make.

27
00:01:04,917 --> 00:01:08,493
Would you excuse me?

28
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:13,271
Sam, get Mr. Levine at Toytown Stores

29
00:01:13,271 --> 00:01:15,449
on the telephone for me, please.

30
00:01:15,449 --> 00:01:20,405
Right.

31
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:25,583
Hello. Susan Stewart calling Mr. Levine, please.

32
00:01:25,583 --> 00:01:29,339
He's on the phone.

33
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:32,317
Mr. Levine, Susan Stewart.

34
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:35,295
I find myself in an embarrassing situation.

35
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:38,273
I made another lunch date for today

36
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:41,251
and forgot to enter it in my appointment book.

37
00:01:41,251 --> 00:01:44,229
Can you and I meet for drinks tomorrow?

38
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:49,647
I'd really appreciate it.... Yes.... Thank you....

39
00:01:49,647 --> 00:01:51,992
Tomorrow at five o'clock at the Biltmore.

40
00:01:51,992 --> 00:01:53,163
I'll see you then.

41
00:01:53,163 --> 00:02:19,964
Thank you, Mr. Levine.

42
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:21,894
Welcome to the South Street restaurant, folks.

43
00:02:21,894 --> 00:02:22,524
What'll it be?

44
00:02:22,524 --> 00:02:22,942
What do you recommend?

45
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:25,609
Well, the crab salad's always a big hit.

46
00:02:25,609 --> 00:02:27,200
Susan, would you like the crab salad?

47
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,898
I'd love the crab salad.

48
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:31,398
Michelle, would you like to try the crab salad, too?

49
00:02:31,398 --> 00:02:32,368
OK, Daddy.

50
00:02:32,368 --> 00:02:34,828
We'll have three crab salads

51
00:02:34,828 --> 00:02:35,154
and a pitcher of lemonade.

52
00:02:35,154 --> 00:02:37,832
Help yourself to celery and carrots and other vegetables.

53
00:02:37,832 --> 00:02:41,722
We used to catch crabs.

54
00:02:41,722 --> 00:02:42,634
Where was that?

55
00:02:42,634 --> 00:02:45,308
We had a summer house on Fire Island.

56
00:02:45,308 --> 00:02:46,766
Do you remember, Michelle?

57
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:47,024
Sure.

58
00:02:47,024 --> 00:02:49,744
You and Mommy used to take me on the ferryboat.

59
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:51,112
Sometimes, at night,

60
00:02:51,112 --> 00:02:54,865
we would go down to the beach and catch crabs,

61
00:02:54,865 --> 00:02:55,065
remember?

62
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:56,540
With a piece of meat on a string!

63
00:02:56,540 --> 00:02:57,700
Right.

64
00:02:57,700 --> 00:03:13,567
Well, I think I'm going to go get us all some vegetables.

65
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:24,165
There you go.

66
00:03:24,165 --> 00:03:25,829
Thank you.

67
00:03:25,829 --> 00:03:31,435
And some ice-cold lemonade.

68
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:32,155
Thank you.

69
00:03:32,155 --> 00:03:33,235
Enjoy it.

70
00:03:33,235 --> 00:03:35,635
Michelle, can I help you with the lemonade?

71
00:03:35,635 --> 00:03:36,302
No, thank you.

72
00:03:36,302 --> 00:03:40,369
I'll wait for my father.

73
00:03:40,369 --> 00:03:43,347
Michelle, can we have a talk?

74
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:49,347
Sure.

75
00:03:49,347 --> 00:03:49,547
I know you miss your mother.

76
00:03:49,347 --> 00:03:49,547
You do?

77
00:03:49,347 --> 00:03:52,281
Yes. And I'm not trying to take her place.

78
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:53,917
Then why are you and Daddy

79
00:03:53,917 --> 00:03:55,259
spending so much time together?

80
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:58,237
Because we like each other.

81
00:03:58,237 --> 00:04:01,215
And right now, he needs a friend.

82
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:02,415
I'm his friend.

83
00:04:02,415 --> 00:04:04,193
I know you are.

84
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:09,171
Sometimes he's very sad.

85
00:04:09,171 --> 00:04:11,149
And so are you, I think.

86
00:04:11,149 --> 00:04:13,127
Sometimes.

87
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:16,105
I'd like to be your friend, too.

88
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:25,038
Will you let me be your friend, Michelle?

89
00:04:25,038 --> 00:04:29,576
So, what were you two talking about?

90
00:04:29,576 --> 00:04:30,994
Just girl talk, Daddy.

91
00:04:30,994 --> 00:04:33,244
It's too hard to explain.

92
00:04:33,244 --> 00:04:33,972
You're probably right.

93
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:36,972
Well, let's get started.
